Fix overlay-scrollbar blinking and teleporting (sprite mode + movement filter).

Device-reported: the overlay thumb blinks (vanishes for frames) and teleports
(jumps position) during scrolling. Root cause analysis of the async scrollbar
path (ScrollerCoordinated, USE(COORDINATED_GRAPHICS_ASYNC_SCROLLBAR)): on
every scroll tick it repaints the whole track texture with Skia Ganesh from
the scrolling thread into a REUSED pooled GL texture, relying on GL fences
for cross-context ordering. This libhybris/Adreno stack does not order those
reliably (the same driver behavior that motivated the gpu-sync conservative
mode), so the compositor intermittently samples the texture's previous pool
contents (a stale thumb = teleport) or its cleared transparent state (blink).

Two env-gated changes, defaults = upstream behavior when unset:

- WEBKIT_SCROLLBAR_SPRITE=1: paint the thumb once into a small CPU-rasterized
  sprite (plain glTexSubImage2D upload, no Ganesh, no per-frame texture churn;
  glFinish fallback when GL fences are unavailable) and move it per scroll
  tick with setContentsRect only — pure compositor geometry, committed on the
  same path as the content scroll position, so there is nothing left to
  desync. Repaints happen only when the thumb length or scrollbar state
  (colors, dark mode, fade opacity) changes. Hovered/pressed/non-overlay
  scrollbars keep the upstream full-track painting path (irrelevant on touch).

- WEBKIT_SCROLLBAR_SMOOTHING=<0..1>: exponential low-pass filter on the
  displayed thumb position, so any residual jump in the scroll data (e.g.
  after a main-thread stall) renders as a fast glide instead of a teleport.
  A single pending catch-up tick on the compositing run loop keeps the glide
  converging when scroll ticks stop; the filter snaps within 1px of target.

deploy/runtime-common.sh sets WEBKIT_SCROLLBAR_SPRITE=1 and
WEBKIT_SCROLLBAR_SMOOTHING=0.4 on device.

